  was not distributed with this file, You can obtain one
  at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

  This file is covered by the PaskalCPP Runtime Exception
  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ldtkloader.pcpp - the ldtkloader unit: `import ldtkloader;` reads LDtk
  projects (https://ldtk.io: .ldtk projects, .ldtkl level files) from
  PaskalCPP. A self-describing vendor module: it owns every include path,
  library path and link library it needs, per official target. The library
  is libLDtkLoader.a (one per target), built by PaskalCPP-Libs'
  build-ldtkloader.cmd from LDtkLoader's own CMake project, linked by
  @linklibrary: every module of the program shares the one copy, and a
  program links only the libraries it imports.

  The API is LDtkLoader's C++ API as it ships
  (https://github.com/Madour/LDtkLoader), used straight from PaskalCPP: an
  `ldtk::Project` variable, LProject.loadFromFile(path) (the project and,
  when it saves its levels separately, every level file it names, found
  relative to the project), then the getters: allWorlds / getWorld (a
  project of one world answers getWorld()), a world's allLevels / getLevel
  (by name, uid or iid), a level's name, size, position, bg_color, fields
  (getField<T>(name)) and allLayers / getLayer(name), a layer's getType
  (ldtk::LayerType::IntGrid, Entities, Tiles, AutoLayer), getName,
  isVisible, getCellSize, getGridSize, getOffset, getOpacity, hasTileset /
  getTileset, allTiles (each an ldtk::Tile: tileId, flipX, flipY, alpha,
  getPosition, getTextureRect), getIntGridVal(x, y) and allEntities /
  getEntitiesByName (each an ldtk::Entity: getName, getPosition, getSize,
  fields through getField<T>(name), T one of int, float, bool,
  std::string, ldtk::Color, ldtk::IntPoint, ldtk::EnumValue,
  ldtk::FilePath, ldtk::EntityRef; a field's value() reads it, is_null()
  tells an empty one). allTilesets / getTileset give each tileset's path
  (relative to the project), tile_size and getTileTexturePos.

  LDtkLoader reports a problem by throwing (an `std::invalid_argument`
  "LDtkLoader exception ...", or the JSON reader's own exception for a file
  that is not valid JSON): a file it cannot open or read, a level, layer,
  entity, tileset or field asked for by a name that is not there. A
  PaskalCPP program catches it with `guard ... except ... end;` (excmsg()
  is the exception's text). A Project, World, Level, Layer or Entity is
  never copied: it is used in place, by const reference (`ptr to const` in
  PaskalCPP), and one Project reads another file with loadFromFile again.
  A project whose JSON version is not LDtkLoader's own major.minor (1.5)
  still loads, with a warning on stdout.

  Files are read with the C++ library's streams, so a program that imports
  HookIO reads projects from an IO or a zip archive as well (ldtk_ext's
  LoadLdtkProjectIO / LoadLdtkProjectZip do that, and draw the levels with
  raylib).
==============================================================================*/

module unit ldtkloader;

@addincludepath "$P:res/libs/vendor/ldtkloader/include";

@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/ldtkloader/lib/x86_64-windows-gnu";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/ldtkloader/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu";
@else
  @message error "ldtkloader: unsupported target";
@endif

@linklibrary "LDtkLoader";

// The headers go to this unit's header, so every importer sees LDtkLoader's
// API (Project.hpp includes every other public header)
cpp header;

#include <LDtkLoader/Project.hpp>

end.
